25,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Rin,,It turns out setting up every morning takes way more time than I thought. It's a real drain.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are rigid. We pay for the space regardless of headcount, and moving wires is expensive.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"There's a clear divide in seat quality, and past shuffles have caused weeks of chaos.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The noise varies wildly across the room, and getting a desk physically right takes days of tweaking.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Sitting together really helps. New people learn faster and we communicate better when we're close.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If we change seats daily, we're just losing minutes every single morning. That's not efficient.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. Frequent changes to the layout will just bleed the budget through facility fees.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"But if we stay fixed, some people are stuck with the worst spots forever. That's unfair.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,Moving frequently is out of the question for me. I can't spend my life readjusting my chair.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Yumi,,But we can't ignore the synergy. Being near the right people makes the work actually happen.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm starting to think stability is better than flexibility if the ""flex"" costs us time.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Stability is the only way to keep the budget under control.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I still worry about the ""bad"" seats, but I see the chaos of shuffling is a problem.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,I'll vote against anything that forces us to move our equipment constantly.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"If we group by function, we get the social benefits and the stability.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
